  "summary": "This file is the English grammar course with the answers translated: most prompts are English fill-in-the-blanks about English grammar (to be, do-support, a/an, has/have, which/who, inversion), hints explain English rules, and cloze items show English sentences, so learners cannot practice Italian grammar. I rewrote each into the equivalent Italian exercise. Several answers are also wrong Italian: present perfect durations rendered as 'ho vissuto qui per', 'Se lo sapessi prima', 'sarebbe stata', 'Non prima era arrivata prima dell'incontro', 'condizioni meteorologiche povere', 'rotto il record', and 'E'' misspellings.",
